bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    u8_array_into_word_array_unchecked_slots_2026-11-28, 0, "Follow-up to seed_jit_u8_array_into_i64_array_param_reads_zero_2026-11-27 (Fable review of the E1003 lane). The [u8]-into-word-array rule rejects call arguments only (fn, later-declared fn, instance/self/static/impl method, trait-typed receiver). Still admitted without diagnostic: (1) let/var with a declared word-array type initialised or reassigned from a [u8] (`var w: [i64] = bytes`), (2) a fn returning [u8] where `-> [i64]` is declared, (3) a [u8] stored into a struct/class field typed [i64]/List<i64>, (4) a [u8] passed to a `[i64]?` parameter, (5) nested `[[u8]]` into `[[i64]]`, (6) a trait-typed receiver whose method name is a builtin collection method (put/push/...): lower_builtin_method_call takes the call first, so the trait row is never consulted, (7) a method call that passes the [u8] through a named argument (`bx.at(data: b, i: 0)`): the method-row check runs only for all-positional, unspread calls. The runtime word-write trap (rt_typed_words_*_set) still catches writes; reads of an admitted [u8] depend on the runtime widening."

