bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    u8_array_into_word_array_unchecked_slots_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 fable fix (work/u8-word-slots-20261128, base release/1.0.0 5e68223f4a7, commits fb8d50a7fb2 + 6c44b2b4b25). reject_array_element_mismatch now also runs on an annotated let/var, an assignment target (local, field, index; an untyped `var w = []` is exempt), a struct/class field initialiser, and an explicit or implicit return. `[i64]?` is checked as its payload, `[[i64]]` by its leaf element (a nested literal row by row), a trait method named like a builtin collection method is checked inside lower_builtin_method_call, and instance/static/trait method calls are followed through named arguments (rows now carry the parameter name). Let and assignment diagnostics name file and line. Red first: 7 tests in hir/lower/tests/function_tests.rs, 29 rejected shapes all lowering on base; green after, plus accept controls (literal, same type, word array into [u8], `.map(\x: x as i64)`). Fallout oracle (seed `compile`, 10196 in-tree .spl: every src/test file mentioning u8/Bytes or a word-array type): 6 files hit, 2 causes. (a) seed bug: untyped_empty_array_locals was keyed by local index and never cleared, so a declared `var z: [u8] = []` was retyped to [i64] by `z.push(0x00)` when an earlier function left the same index marked (gcm_gf128_mul via tls_common_hooks); now saved/restored per function, regression test added. (b) five buffers initialised from text.bytes() (typed [i64] by the seed) then reassigned from [u8]-returning helpers now declare [u8] (native_build_argv_v1, native_build_full_abi_v1, native_build_payload_codec_v1). Final seed: 0 [u8] hits; the 463 files that still fail lowering report the identical first error on the base seed. Rust: compiler lib failure set identical to base (15 pre-existing; 5293 passed vs 5286). Specs of the touched modules pass on both seeds. Perf (compile, alternated rounds, base d2c93746b106 vs new 7494bad4717f): scv/parser.spl 5 rounds mean 1.890s vs 1.868s; app/cli/bootstrap_main.spl 8 rounds user mean 18.66s vs 18.73s (+0.4%), min 16.24s vs 16.06s; RSS equal. Not covered: files outside the oracle set (37009 .spl mention neither u8 nor a word-array type), the pure interpreter lane (lowering-based rule), a [u8] pushed into a [[i64]] via builtin push, and untyped list relays. The pure-Simple compiler (src/compiler) has no such rule to mirror."

